:44,"event":{"type":"answer_delta","text":"An encyclopedia article states ISS routes power"}},{"dt":48,"event":{"type":"answer_delta","text":" from four solar-array wings through four Main"}},{"dt":38,"event":{"type":"answer_delta","text":" Bus Switching Units in the S0 truss"}},{"dt":45,"event":{"type":"answer_delta","text":", each distributing to two of eight channels"}},{"dt":41,"event":{"type":"answer_delta","text":" [WEB-1]. An agency site"}},{"dt":48,"event":{"type":"answer_delta","text":" reports MBSU-3 failure"}},{"dt":42,"event":{"type":"answer_delta","text":" reduced station power"}},{"dt":98,"event":{"type":"answer_delta","text":" by about 25%, triggering a"}},{"dt":19,"event":{"type":"answer_delta","text":" robotic failover/replacement operation [WEB"}},{"dt":48,"event":{"type":"answer_delta","text":"-2]."}},{"dt":201,"event":{"type":"usage","usage":{"label":"answer","role":"answer","model":"muse-spark-1.3","effort":"high","ms":68775,"promptTokens":5190,"completionTokens":8559,"reasoningTokens":7892,"costUsd":0.04286325}}},{"dt":3,"event":{"type":"answer","markdown":"**Diagnosis**\nPrimary bus A short on M-04 at t=90 s, breaker tripped 120 V → 0 V [FE-0814]. TM-M04-BUS reads 0 V vs nominal 120 V, residual -120, lo 100, down from 120 V at t=83 s to 0 V at t=91 s, trend -31.31 per min, projection crosses null over 6000 s horizon [TM-M04-BUS]. Failover to bus B complete at t=91 s, compute capped at 48 % (bus B 3.6 kW) [FE-0815]. M-04 is Gen-1 dual 120 V buses A/B with PDU SN PD-0433 reworked under NCR-0412 [BLD-M04]. PDU harness potted, PDU NOT field-replaceable, overriding FRU-PDU-01, disposition use as is, swap module if PDU fails [NCR-0412] [FRU-PDU-01]. Bus B alone carried 3.6 kW for 72 h stable within ±0.4 V, util capped at 48 %, no hazard on single-bus operation [TR-0977]. Without action M-04 stays capped at 48 % on bus B with no hazard per test but unrepairable without module swap [TR-0977] [NCR-0412]. Undock requires drained module util 0 % [ICD-DOCK-01].\n**What the cameras show**\nCAM-2 close-up at 4 m shows bright sparking particle plume erupting from center of PDU panel on underside of module [CAM-2]. Plume extends about panel-width outward with no separate holes or scorch visible on surrounding body, grapple fixture not distinctly visible so clearance cannot be confirmed in this view [CAM-2]. SAM 3.1 on CAM-3 targeted SEG-1 confidence 0.88 on M-04 at point [-0.03,-0.01,15.6], nearest feature grapple at distance 0.03 [SEG-1] [CAM-3]. Closest grasp SEG-1 is 1.76 m from shorted PDU, ≥ 0.5 m keepout [SEG-1].\n**Decision**\nMIGRATE_WORKLOADS M-04 to M-03, M-05, M-10, auto: deadline none, next contact t=1320 s.\nSWAP_MODULE M-04 with S-1 using SEG-1, gated: deadline none, next contact t=1320 s, no hazard deadline before AOS 1320 s, waits for operator approval, S-1 Gen-2, 2.4× perf/kW [TR-1302], failure becomes upgrade.\n**Public precedent**\nAn encyclopedia article states ISS routes power from four solar-array wings through four Main Bus Switching Units in the S0 truss, each distributing to two of eight channels [WEB-1]. An agency site reports MBSU-3 failure reduced station power by about 25%, triggering a robotic failover/replacement operation [WEB-2].","citations":[{"type":"event","id":"FE-0814","label":"Primary bus A short: breaker tripped, 120 V → 0 V"},{"type":"telemetry","id":"TM-M04-BUS","label":"TM-M04-BUS (FDIR channel)"},{"type":"event","id":"FE-0815","label":"Failover to bus B complete; compute capped at 48 % (bus B 3.6 kW)"},{"type":"record","id":"NCR-0412","label":"PDU harness potted during rework: PDU not field-replaceable"},{"type":"record","id":"BLD-M04","label":"M-04 build traveler"},{"type":"record","id":"FRU-PDU-01","label":"Power distribution unit: field-replaceable unit (generic catalogue)"},{"type":"record","id":"TR-0977","label":"M-04 single-bus endurance test"},{"type":"record","id":"ICD-DOCK-01","label":"Module-to-truss docking interface"},{"type":"camera","id":"CAM-2","label":"Damage site close-up, 4 m"},{"type":"camera","id":"CAM-3","label":"Grapple fixture + latch B, 4 m"},{"type":"segment","id":"SEG-1","label":"grapple fixture (matched as \"circle\") in CAM-3"},{"type":"record","id":"TR-1302","label":"mentioned by propose_action"},{"type":"web","id":"WEB-1","label":"Maintenance of the International Space Station","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maintenance_of_the_International_Space_Station"},{"type":"web","id":"WEB-2","label":"nasa.gov","url":"https://www.nasa.gov/centers-and-facilities/johnson/robotics-work-successful-station-returned-to-full-power/"}],"unknownIds":[],"numbers":{"checked":17,"unsupported":[]}}},{"dt":0,"event":{"type":"done","totals":{"promptTokens":45132,"completionTokens":20235,"costUsd":0.14759875,"toolCalls":7,"ms":162278}}}]